			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> 🤩</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109383010146269992",
			"parentId": "109382955679916642",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany/109383009920246789",
			"author": {
				"name": "François REMY",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/297/345/151/441/917/original/837e168bda7c4922.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-21T17:37:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Oh, I don't know if they cost anything, I'm just asking for your experience here to learn more about what you did.</p><p>Do you care for instance about your retweets, or just your own tweets?</p><p>I find that backing up your retweets / quoted tweets / likes is the most difficult, I was wondering if you had any thoughts on this already.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109383023473862834",
			"parentId": "109383010146269992",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109383023473862834",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-21T17:41:22.210Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>FremyCompany</span></a></span> I do back up retweets, although the content is truncated e.g. <a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/twitter/1587076514939641856/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">zachleat.com/twitter/158707651</span><span class=\"invisible\">4939641856/</span></a></p><p>quote tweets link directly to the source <a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/twitter/1586436147386888193/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">zachleat.com/twitter/158643614</span><span class=\"invisible\">7386888193/</span></a></p><p>My concern with the retweet thing is that they don’t really obey norms around upstream deletes</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109383073866724559",
			"parentId": "109383023473862834",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany/109383073435044248",
			"author": {
				"name": "François REMY",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/297/345/151/441/917/original/837e168bda7c4922.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-21T17:54:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yes, because of the truncation (which often deletes the attached media and expanded urls), I am currently recrawling all of them myself (masquerading as the twitter website on my PC).</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109383078907208898",
			"parentId": "109383073866724559",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany/109383078791685240",
			"author": {
				"name": "François REMY",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@FremyCompany",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/297/345/151/441/917/original/837e168bda7c4922.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-21T17:55:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> But for now, I'm only thinking about keeping that data private, but it's interesting to think about the issue of keeping backups of other people's messages that they can't delete easily.</p><p>I will keep this in mind if I want to host this later on, thanks for the thought!</p><p>Any other challenge like this you encountered?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
